1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,700
Can an AI detect your true emotion just from the tone of your voice?

2
00:00:04,099 --> 00:00:07,599
Most speech models cheat by memorizing speaker voices.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,300
Here is how we solved it with PyTorch.

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:14,519
If you split speech data at random, your accuracy is fiction.

5
00:00:14,919 --> 00:00:18,519
We enforced a strict speaker-independent split on twenty-four actors,

6
00:00:18,719 --> 00:00:21,519
testing only on completely unseen voices.

7
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:27,700
We engineered a 280-dimensional acoustic feature vector,

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,200
capturing 40 MFCC bands, pitch velocity, and spectral contrast,

9
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,299
trained with a deep 1D Convolutional Neural Network.

10
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,759
Here is the live project!

11
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:39,859
Featuring live three-second microphone recording with animated waveforms,

12
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:43,260
instant emotion prediction, and a recordings history deck.

13
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:46,370
We delivered honest benchmark metrics.

14
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:49,470
High arousal overlaps between anger and joy,

15
00:00:49,570 --> 00:00:52,970
while subtle sadness shares acoustic prosody with calm speech.

16
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:55,090
Thank you for watching!

17
00:00:55,289 --> 00:00:59,289
Speech Emotion Recognition delivers deep acoustic intelligence for real-world voice signals.

18
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:03,390
Connect on LinkedIn to discuss the project!

